Rules:
  [A1] Use RBAC for role-based access control.
  [A2] Implement least privilege principle.
  [A3] Verify authorization on server side.
  [A4] Use ABAC for attribute-based policies.
  [A5] Audit all authorization decisions.
  [A6] Use deny-by-default policy.
  [A7] Implement separation of duties.
  [A8] Use fine-grained permissions for sensitive operations.

Pros:
  - Security
  - Compliance
  - Flexibility

Cons:
  - Complexity
  - Maintenance overhead
  - Performance impact

Alternatives:
  - ACL
  - ACLs with roles
  - Policy engines (OPA)

